1
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,920
Try stepping back a little

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,620
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling you

3
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
holding Gā-chan's hand

4
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:42,500
That strange feeling I had back then

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,720
So on the arcade guide tiles

6
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black tiles

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten

9
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:09,100
the arrogant-faced politicians
and the blue-eyeshadowed aunties too

10
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,660
Why not turn at that corner over there

11
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone

12
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:27,800
There's Kame-ari! Surely there's Kame-ari!

13
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you

15
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,500
Totally outrageous body jack!

16
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:49,020
How about a drink with me, Nakagawa?

17
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:52,040
I'd love to, senpai,
but I've got something today.

18
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,300
Well, it's just that...

19
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:56,740
I'm having dinner with Cameron Roberts.

20
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,720
She's in Japan to promote
a movie our company produced.

21
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:04,040
The number one popular Hollywood actress?

22
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:04,760
Yes.

23
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,260
Lucky you.

24
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,720
I'm a huge, huge, huge, huge fan of hers.

25
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:12,620
I met her last year at a
home party at her house, too.

26
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:14,360
She's really down-to-earth.

27
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,440
Is that so?

28
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,140
Then, I'll give Reiko your regards.

29
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,340
Wow, you two are amazing.

30
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,120
Knowing a world-famous celebrity,
I'm thrilled.

31
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,300
I'll tell everyone when I get home.

32
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,620
I met her at her home party last year, too.

33
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:33,540
She's really down-to-earth.

34
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:34,440
I see.

35
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:37,120
Then, I'll pass along your regards to Reiko.

36
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,400
Amazing.

37
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:42,720
Both of you knowing a world-famous celebrity,
I'm thrilled.

38
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,920
Screw that!

39
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:55,140
A full course with a
famous Hollywood actress,

40
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:57,860
or sitting face-to-face with
the yakitori shop old man?

41
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:59,460
Don't say that, Ryo-san.

42
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,140
Those two are rich from birth, you know.

43
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:05,220
Their own effort has nothing to do with it.

44
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:08,080
How can the world be this unfair?

45
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,020
Now, now.

46
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:14,220
Since there's a gap in the schedule, I swapped
Nakagawa's electronic planner for a bribe, though.

47
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:17,380
Judging a racing queen contest,
a party for the Forty-Seven Ronin,

48
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:20,500
there's a whole lineup of
dinners with celebrities.

49
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:28,740
It makes me sick how different we are.
Cameron Roberts.

50
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:31,980
This woman is Cameron Roberts

51
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:43,980
Body Snatchers. Your body may
already belong to someone else.

52
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:51,520
Body snatchers Even I'd like to switch bodies with Nakagawa if I could.
Old man, another round!

53
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,840
...the 13th one, bro.

54
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:07,200
I wonder how it got up there.

55
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,980
It must have climbed up
and can't get back down.

56
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,020
Ryotsu, it's your turn.

57
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:13,000
What do you want me to do?

58
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,380
You're the one who can save it, after all.

59
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:16,720
I'm counting on you.

60
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,440
No matter what happens,
you protect the cat's life.

61
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,260
Given the circumstances,
some sacrifice can't be helped.

62
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:23,420
Sacrifice?

63
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:27,200
You want me to sacrifice
myself for one measly cat?

64
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,820
What do you mean, "measly"?

65
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:31,940
The kitty matters a lot
more than the likes of you.

66
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:32,700
That's the general idea.

67
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:36,560
What did you just do up there?! You bastard!
Did you screw up?! Calm down! Please, calm down!

68
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:37,780
Senior Constable Ryotsu!

69
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:38,640
Y-yes!

70
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,760
Stop making excuses and get going!

71
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:42,760
Understood!

72
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:50,340
Come on, hurry up!

73
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:52,220
Yes, now come along without
causing any more trouble!

74
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:54,600
Watch out!

75
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:01,760
Are you all right?

76
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,160
Nakagawa-san!

77
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,520
You shouldn't move him.

78
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,380
Somebody, quick, call an ambulance!

79
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:16,840
Why am I lying on the ground?

80
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,480
But I'm right here.

81
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:23,340
I'm telling you, Ryotsu.

82
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:24,380
Ryotsu.

83
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:26,560
Yeah, stop saying weird things!

84
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:28,680
Just look at this carefully.

85
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:32,800
My face is on Senpai's face.

86
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,320
What are you fooling around for?

87
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,860
I'm not fooling around.

88
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:37,180
I'm Nakagawa.

89
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,080
From the shock of colliding with Senpai,

90
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,880
our bodies got swapped.

91
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:41,580
No way.

92
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:43,440
Can such a thing really happen?

93
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,560
It's hard to believe,

94
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,980
but when I watch the way he talks and acts,

95
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,040
Oh my god, what a thing.

96
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,920
So that makes me the senior, then?

97
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:53,240
Please hang in there.

98
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,760
I just called an ambulance.

99
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:57,240
A helicopter would be faster.

100
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:59,000
It's me, Keiichi.

101
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:01,120
My voice sounds strange?

102
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,920
This is no time to be talking about that.

103
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,740
Get an emergency medical
helicopter here right away!

104
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,160
Senpai, please hang in there, senpai.

105
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:19,300
Chief, I'll go along too.

106
00:06:19,660 --> 00:06:20,320
Leave it to you.

107
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:25,860
He doesn't really seem
like the real Nakagawa.

108
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:29,100
It really feels like we've swapped bodies.

109
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:31,680
Ryotsu could never pull
off something like this.

110
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:34,840
Hard as it is to believe, that is Nakagawa.

111
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:44,360
There are no external injuries,
and his brain waves are normal.

112
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,340
I don't think there's
any particular problem.

113
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:50,180
But why would he be in an underground
isolation facility like this?

114
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,540
Please think about it.

115
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,600
Although he looks like me,

116
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,080
inside, he's Kankichi Ryotsu.

117
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,440
I'm talking about Senpai.

118
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,260
Once he wakes up and
realizes he's gotten my body,

119
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,640
he'll surely pose as me

120
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:02,740
and do something outrageous for sure.

121
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:03,580
I see.

122
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:06,420
A man named Ryotsu would be capable of that.

123
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,900
So I'm sorry, Senpai,

124
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:11,480
but we have no choice but to
confine him here for a while.

125
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,220
Please keep it a secret that he's here.

126
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:14,960
Understood.

127
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:18,480
What? The President's body swapped?

128
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:19,380
Yes.

129
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:23,340
Apparently, it's professionally
called a soul separation phenomenon.

130
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,920
There are also many
eyewitnesses at the scene,

131
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:30,260
and he knows the President's
private matters very well too.

132
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:34,760
Well then, President,
by the way, today's schedule is -

133
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:39,920
Today, it's Prince Hepelovsky, an agriculture professor,
and an appreciation of traditional Japanese culture.

134
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,540
After that, there's the dance
party at the embassy, right?

135
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,820
Pardon me.

136
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:48,780
To rattle off a schedule that only the President should know,
so smoothly...

137
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,620
There's no doubt about it,
you're definitely the President.

138
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,140
It's fine, don't worry about it.

139
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,960
As long as you believe me, that's all I ask.

140
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:00,980
Yes!

141
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:02,640
I finally became Nakagawa!

142
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:05,760
Good thing I swapped
Nakagawa's electronic organizer!

143
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:08,160
What perfect timing that collision was.

144
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:10,000
I can't let this chance slip away.

145
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,420
So now I can live a life
of luxury and extravagance.

146
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:35,860
After this, let's see,

147
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:38,680
you have an interview with
Weekly Cafe Das, right?

148
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:39,260
Yes.

149
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:39,580
Yes.

150
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,140
Noriko-san is such a friendly person.

151
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:46,980
Man, this is a problem.

152
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:54,200
I'm Keiji.

153
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:57,020
Let me out of here!

154
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:58,260
He's saying it again, that guy.

155
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:02,120
I hear Kankichi Ryotsu is quite the character,
you know.

156
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:06,000
Why are you locking me
away in a place like this?

157
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,920
I can't believe such a story.

158
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:09,680
Without any clear proof,

159
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:13,120
we can't just accept that
person as the president.

160
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,460
What do you all think?

161
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:19,760
Understood, understood.

162
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,600
Then how about this?

163
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:24,620
Why don't we have an expert
in the field make the judgment?

164
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,040
An expert in the field.

165
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,560
Is there really such a person?

166
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:27,900
Yes.

167
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,800
I have some idea who that might be.

168
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:34,680
Good morning.

169
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:35,540
Good morning.

170
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,140
You're early, Ryo-chan.

171
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:39,340
Wait, you're Kei-chan, aren't you?

172
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:42,680
Don't mix me up, Reiko-san!

173
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:45,200
That's Ryo-chan's seat.

174
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,200
Where was my seat again?

175
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:53,920
You're always digging around for something over there,
aren't you?

176
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:57,140
Was it like this, then?

177
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:01,080
Here you go, Kei-chan. Coffee.

178
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,580
Coffee? Isn't it green tea?

179
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:06,440
Only Ryo-chan drinks green tea.

180
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:10,480
I figured green tea might
be nice once in a while...

181
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:14,620
Good morning.

182
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:16,080
Good morning.

183
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:18,420
I mean... Ryotsu no, Nakagawa.

184
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:20,680
Nakagawa, are you all right physically?

185
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,220
Yes, I'm fine.

186
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,760
How about Ryotsu?

187
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,740
Well, it seems he hit his head badly.

188
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:30,200
So he's going to be hospitalized
at our clinic for a while.

189
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,400
Then I'll go visit him sometime.

190
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,940
No, that won't be necessary.

191
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:37,400
Excuse me.

192
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,380
Did something happen?

193
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,380
President, actually, I have a favor to ask.

194
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:42,780
What is it, anyway?

195
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:46,360
We'd like the president to take a test
to prove whether he's the real president.

196
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:48,500
Sure, no problem.

197
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:59,160
Hello, everybody, nice party!

198
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,460
Professor Eda

199
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:04,180
Yes, long time no see.
Where have you been all this time?

200
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,240
Please don't ask me that.

201
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:13,040
From the North Pole to the South Pole,
the whole world needs me.

202
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:17,080
This time,
this teacher will be taking the test.

203
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:21,440
And now, the invention of
genius scientist Korosuke Ezaki.

204
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:29,820
With this lie detector, we'll be able to tell whether
Gorilla-kun's body really contains Nakagawa-kun's soul.

205
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:38,780
With this machine, we'll know with 100%
certainty whether it's real or fake.

206
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,200
Then, please.

207
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:43,860
Gorilla-kun, are you ready?

208
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:47,080
I'm Keiichi Nakagawa, you know.

209
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:51,340
Just joking!
It's an Indonesian joke to loosen you up.

210
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:53,160
Now let's get started!

211
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:07,380
Let's get started right away!

212
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:11,780
You'll answer every question
within two seconds, got it?

213
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,700
Then, question one.

214
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:17,240
Your favorite Japanese sweet is...

215
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:19,100
Japanese sweets.

216
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:21,020
Answer within two seconds.

217
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,680
Monaka, it's monaka!

218
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,680
Now the next question.

219
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,740
Leaning bamboo against a bamboo fence,
because I wanted to lean bamboo?

220
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:36,980
Which is easier to say: red scrolls,
blue scrolls, or wooden scrolls?

221
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:39,160
What kind of question is that?

222
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:40,120
Within two seconds!

223
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:43,300
Red curly hair, red curly curly curly.

224
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,200
Blue curly hair, red curly curly curly.

225
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,800
Blue curly hair, red curly curly curly.

226
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,960
Yellow curly hair.

227
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,340
This is torture!

228
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,340
If you were a cat,

229
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:55,780
where would your favorite spot be?

230
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:56,620
The veranda.

231
00:12:56,620 --> 00:12:58,420
Permed hair or a crew cut.

232
00:12:58,420 --> 00:12:59,400
Which is more manly?

233
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,480
Crew cut.

234
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,880
Pro wrestling, sumo, or...
which do you like best?

235
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:03,460
And cake?

236
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:05,460
Now, the final question.

237
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:09,540
Tap-dancing dog!

238
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:13,980
Time's up!

239
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,960
The answer is in!

240
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:26,700
This person is definitely Nakagawa Keiichi!

241
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:35,440
But how?
Why can you say that so definitively?

242
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:41,100
The answers naturally emerge
from among all the questions.

243
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,400
Take this first question, for example.

244
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:46,220
The answer to
"What's your favorite Japanese sweet?"

245
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:47,720
Yes, it was monaka!

246
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:50,380
So what does this tell us?

247
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:53,780
The "naka" inside monaka is the
"naka" in Nakagawa.

248
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:57,280
Then there's the answer to
"If you were a cat..."

249
00:13:57,280 --> 00:14:01,080
The "gawa" in engawa is the
"gawa" in Nakagawa.

250
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,140
And the favorite is K1.

251
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:06,800
Keiichi.

252
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:11,740
In other words, he's unconsciously
confessing who he really is.

253
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:14,420
And the clincher is the
answer to the last question.

254
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:17,760
The pun on "A Dog of Flanders
" is "A Dog of Hula Dance."

255
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:24,760
This hyper-sense is something only Nakagawa,
who lived abroad for so long, could have.

256
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:29,580
So the gorilla-looking guy
right in front of us is definitely

257
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,060
Nakagawa Keiichi.

258
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:37,040
We're thoroughly impressed, Professor.

259
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,360
With this, we can persuade the executives.

260
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:42,680
Well, for me, this is a piece of cake.

261
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:45,980
I was sure it was Nakagawa all along, too.

262
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:47,640
Yeah, I thought so too.

263
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:48,940
Right? Right?

264
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:49,660
Hey.

265
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:53,720
I keep telling you, I'm Nakagawa Keiichi!

266
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:55,800
He's persistent, isn't he?

267
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,720
He'll give up eventually.

268
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,820
Really,
I'm glad it turned out to be the president.

269
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:04,640
It's only natural.

270
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:07,220
Thanks to that bumbling professor,
we're saved.

271
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:11,440
On the flip side, it's like we've
got an official seal of approval now.

272
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:20,360
Apparently a five-sun nail is
sticking out right in the middle, so

273
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,920
they said I had to come all
the way here just to sweep up.

274
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:28,640
Eeeeeeeh!

275
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:32,260
Hahaha.

276
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:33,520
Reiko

277
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:36,400
Hey.

278
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,080
Dadada!

279
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,460
Dadada!

280
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:40,120
Dadada!

281
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:45,840
Nyahahaha!

282
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:54,040
What did I ever do to deserve this?

283
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:57,080
Why do I have to go through this?

284
00:15:58,820 --> 00:16:00,200
It's gone quiet, hasn't it?

285
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,820
So you've finally given up.

286
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,840
That president...

287
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,560
What is it?

288
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:09,560
About that matter we've been
pursuing in America and Europe...

289
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:11,060
That matter.

290
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:15,560
Yes, I'd like your specific instructions
as president of the Nakagawa Group.

291
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:18,320
That matter... you mean that one?

292
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,620
If it's that one,
then go for it in a big way.

293
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:22,220
Go for it with gusto, all out!

294
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:27,120
President, you really need
to look over these documents.

295
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,380
Just take a look at them, will you?

296
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:31,180
President, how should we handle this matter?

297
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:32,460
Just leave it to me, whatever.

298
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:34,840
About that matter...

299
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:37,200
Shut up already. Just let them do whatever they want,
that's all.

300
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:39,480
President.

301
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:40,940
W-what is it?

302
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:44,180
Regarding that matter,
I handled it just as you instructed, and...

303
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:46,400
the dollar and the euro both crashed.

304
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:49,880
The global economy is in chaos,
as if it were hit by a tsunami.

305
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:52,080
Is that a problem?

306
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,000
Of course it is!

307
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:58,560
Since this is a good opportunity, President!
I'd like to restore your disordered lifestyle of late to how it was before!

308
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:02,160
W-what's this?

309
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:04,820
You always used to call me within an hour.

310
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:07,720
Ah, y-yes, that's right.

311
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:11,220
From now on, you'll be carrying
out your schedule exactly as planned.

312
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:14,270
Yes, at 10 o'clock,
a regular meeting in Ginza,

313
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:17,680
at 11:30, an inspection of
computer-related facilities in Sendai,

314
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:21,660
at 1 o'clock, entertaining the presidents
of 150 overseas branch companies in Kyoto.

315
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,100
Wait a moment,
I'd like to go shopping though...

316
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,100
Unfortunately,

317
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:26,920
there isn't a single second to spare.

318
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:30,760
Rooster rillettes with béarnaise sauce

319
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,680
Andouillette with red wine flavor,
anchoïade-style

320
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:36,480
Scallops Marielle-style, autumn twilight

321
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:38,860
Lamb brains, peeled

322
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:41,540
Got it, that's enough explanation.

323
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:42,360
Yes.

324
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:48,680
Once in a while, I'd like to try some
common people's ramen or something.

325
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:50,840
That's not on the schedule.

326
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,480
Aaaaaah!

327
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:59,960
You won't be seeing it properly now.
They say there's no cassis.

328
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:00,980
Wh -

329
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:32,100
Is that so? Senpai really said that?

330
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,660
No matter what, that's going too far.

331
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:35,540
Let's teach him a lesson.

332
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:46,040
Geez, being Nakagawa isn't exactly easy.

333
00:18:46,040 --> 00:19:04,880
Good morning, this is Nakagawa.

334
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:07,620
Please be careful.

335
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:14,840
No, Senpai's body has short legs,
so it's hard to drive.

336
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:17,060
Hey, that's Ryotsu's seat!

337
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:22,000
No, no, I don't know why,
but since my body is Senpai's, I just...

338
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:27,060
That's right,
I heard Ryo-chan is coming to work today.

339
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:29,560
Did that guy get discharged
from the hospital?

340
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:30,700
That guy.

341
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:32,580
No, no, Senpai...

342
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:33,140
That's right.

343
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:36,820
Just as Nakagawa said,
what was inside was completely Ryotsu!

344
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:38,640
What is going on?

345
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:51,100
I cleaned out the all-rotation machine
at Kameari 2-chome in just 30 minutes.

346
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:53,040
Are you Ryotsu?

347
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:56,640
How dare you call your senior "you"!

348
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,680
Sorry, sorry.

349
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:02,600
Nakagawa, you've been getting cocky lately,
you know that?

350
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,040
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

351
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:08,000
Nakagawa, lend me 100,000 yen.

352
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,400
I've got a sure-win bet lined up.

353
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:14,080
I don't carry cash on me, you know.

354
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,920
You've got a card, right?

355
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,700
I'm borrowing it for two or three days.

356
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,000
Hey, Ryotsu.

357
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:19,560
Yes.

358
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:23,140
You were here?

359
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:25,800
If you're here,
you should've said so from the start!

360
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:28,740
Damn, we were so close!

361
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,340
What are you lot looking at?

362
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:34,460
We'll wait.

363
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,360
Honestly, kids these days...

364
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,120
Hey, Reiko, tea.

365
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:38,960
Yes.

366
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:43,600
We had an important race today, didn't we?

367
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,960
It's completely me, there are two of me now.

368
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:49,900
So where on earth did Nakagawa go?

369
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:50,920
Hey, Ryotsu!

370
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:51,460
Yes?

371
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:53,720
You're not Ryo-chan, are you?

372
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:59,120
Have I always treated Nakagawa this badly?

373
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:02,340
I hear you cleaned out Ryo's room, Ryotsu.

374
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:05,040
Yeah, I finally woke up to myself, you know.

375
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:08,020
I threw out all the model
kits and figures you collected.

376
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:08,800
What?

377
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:12,260
Hey, those were valuable assets!

378
00:21:12,260 --> 00:21:14,940
It's none of your business, so shut up!

379
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,580
Sorry about that

380
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,820
While you're at it,
get rid of those filthy videos too.

381
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:21,900
Yeah, true.

382
00:21:21,900 --> 00:21:24,800
Wait, don't give advice without asking.

383
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,800
Why is Kei-chan coming up?

384
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,980
Yeah, I was talking to Ryo-san.

385
00:21:28,980 --> 00:21:32,960
So, as for me, I mean, I think it'd
be better not to throw them away.

386
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:35,560
Hey, senior,
it'd be a waste to throw them out.

387
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:37,660
Besides,
I'm already tired of these adult videos.

388
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:41,520
Ken-chan did?

389
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,600
No way, really?

390
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:45,520
What should I do... Yeah, just sell them.

391
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:47,600
No, senior, absolutely not.

392
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:51,000
I'll buy them all,
the whole lot for 1 million yen.

393
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,420
Ugh, you pervert.

394
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:55,800
Hey, hey, so please, just throw them away.

395
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:58,720
Hey, I never said that, Nakagawa-kun.

396
00:21:58,720 --> 00:21:59,940
Yeah, just sell them all.

397
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:02,840
No, I said no, don't throw them away.

398
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:14,320
Damn it, I knew something was off! These guys were in on it together,
tricking me!

399
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,040
Professor Ezaki.

400
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:21,200
What is it this time?

401
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:25,020
Genius scientist Korosuke
Ezaki's heartfelt new invention!

402
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:27,960
This is the personality swap machine!

403
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:30,760
Appearances stay the same,
but only the personalities switch places.

404
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:34,700
In other words, we can change
Gorilla-kun and Nakagawa-kun back.

405
00:22:37,700 --> 00:22:38,520
I see.

406
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:41,120
If we can really swap places
with Nakagawa with this,

407
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:43,260
I can do whatever I want, out in the open.

408
00:22:43,900 --> 00:22:46,220
That's great, isn't it, senpai?

409
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:48,500
With this,
we might be able to go back to normal.

410
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:49,480
Yeah, that's right.

411
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:52,060
The senior who switched us back

412
00:22:52,060 --> 00:22:52,980
I'm a little scared, you know.

413
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:53,560
Just do it already.

414
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:58,200
Nakagawa, no, no, no!

415
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,280
I'm so happy.

416
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:01,680
This means we'll be back to normal!

417
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:03,280
Then, Professor, please.

418
00:23:04,700 --> 00:23:05,820
OK, OK!

419
00:23:06,020 --> 00:23:06,820
Switch!

420
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:11,300
M-move! Get out of the way! This idiot...

421
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:12,680
Aaaaaaah!

422
00:23:19,580 --> 00:23:21,780
What is this?

423
00:23:22,020 --> 00:23:24,620
Why do I have to look like this!

424
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:27,240
Whoa, my body's right over there!

425
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:30,220
Why have I turned into
such a dull-looking man!

426
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:32,780
The insides have turned bad!

427
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:35,480
We're going to be dealt with!

428
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,560
Ryotsu!

429
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:38,280
Because of you, I'm...

430
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:40,060
Senpai, what on earth is happening to me?

431
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:44,900
Why are you imitating me like this!

432
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:47,100
I won't be fooled by that!

433
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:49,820
Professor,
can't you do something about this?

434
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:50,660
No, that's not it!

435
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:52,560
Don't tell me!

436
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:53,460
I'll go!

437
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:56,800
Professor Ezaki,
then please take care of our Ryo.

438
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:58,840
Meow! I'll do anything, meow!

439
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:05,500
Kick the alarm clock,
my pinky toe goes ow-ow-ow.

440
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:13,900
Quickly draw on the eyebrows,
then dash, dash, dash to the station.

441
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:19,360
Packed train,
a quick nap on a salaryman's back.

442
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:25,680
Another rough week,
your demands are quite reasonable.

443
00:24:26,940 --> 00:24:30,500
But I'm getting it done with one hand.

444
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:33,300
Beef bowl, extra sauce, cloudy.

445
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:36,460
The irritation of endless overtime,

446
00:24:37,060 --> 00:24:40,200
cleared right up with more irritation.

447
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:46,480
Every day is no-problem brain

448
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:49,980
After passing through a hot shower,

449
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:53,160
every day is no-problem brain

450
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:56,560
energy restored with a sleep-pillow

451
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:02,480
Every day is no program

452
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:06,180
I love a girl like me

453
00:25:06,180 --> 00:25:09,160
every day is no program

454
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:12,980
Monday with hearts flying around

455
00:25:12,980 --> 00:25:17,040
Monday, Monday, no program

456
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:22,360
What? Axe gets in when you're sweating...

457
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:24,400
This golden bowl has been stolen!

458
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:27,480
Honestly, Terai, while I was napping

459
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:30,360
this happened because
you went off on patrol!

460
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:33,880
If the golden bowl doesn't turn up,
it's all your fault!

461
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:36,720
Next time: Terai, a relentless pursuit!

462
00:25:37,260 --> 00:25:37,880
See you then!

463
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:40,520
Over there, Kame-ari!

464
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:43,960
Well, surely Kame-ari!

465
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:49,100
Come on over, to our town!

466
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:50,660
Thank you!

467
00:25:53,160 --> 00:25:53,940
Thank you for watching.

